    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR01, 0U, "DR-01-RS-0001", "Disk Recovery Index", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_DR01_DISK_RECOVERY_INDEX, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_T001, NULL, 0U, "DISK 144 RECOVERY INDEX\n\nThe medium contains a partial archive of a Government Department of Records Site during its final closure period. Recoverable material includes administrative records, reconstructed rooms, physical-object references and cross-linked evidence.\n\nThe archive is incomplete by design. Restore collections, inspect reconstructed physical material and distinguish what the archive claims from what the surviving physical record can establish.\n\nWHAT VERSION OF THE TRUTH ARE YOU WILLING TO ACCEPT?" },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR01, 1U, "DR-01-RS-0002", "Terminal Access & Command Reference", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "GDR ARCHIVE RECOVERY TERMINAL\n\nINITIATE starts archive services for the current recovery. LIST shows collections currently available. RESTORE <CODE> reconstructs an available collection, subject to the recovery quota. OPEN <RECORD-ID> opens a recovered readable record. EXIT returns to the reconstructed Site.\n\nCommands operate only on material present on Disk 144. A missing record is not evidence that the original record never existed." },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR01, 2U, "DR-01-RS-0003", "Collection Restoration", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "COLLECTION RESTORATION\n\nRecovered collections contribute reconstruction data to the Site. Restoration is persistent for the current recovery and cannot be undone. The available collection pool intentionally exceeds one complete recovery, so choices made during the session can change which material becomes available before the reconstruction reaches 100 percent.\n\nRestoration reconstructs archived state. It does not invent absent information." },
    { FLOPPY144_COLLECTION_DR01, 3U, "DR-01-RS-0004", "Listing & Opening Records", FLOPPY144_DOCUMENT_VIEW_GENERIC, FLOPPY144_TRIGGER_COUNT, NULL, 0U, "LISTING & OPENING RECORDS\n\nLIST presents the collections known to the recovery environment. Each restored collection may contain generated catalogue entries and a smaller number of readable authored records. OPEN accepts a stable record identifier.\n\nCatalogue metadata may survive even where document content does not. Such entries are shown as unavailable rather than silently reconstructed." },
